  "testable_hypotheses_or_predictions": [
    "The evaluation of architectural fluency, complexity, and naturalistic patterns can be measured through sensory-motor responses.",
    "Aesthetic experience of space is influenced by familiarity, expectations, context, and cultural meaning.",
    "The interaction between sensory-motor and knowledge-meaning systems determines complex emotional valuation, moderated by the emotion valuation system."
  ],
  "bridge_warrants": [
    "The aesthetic triad framework integrates neuroaesthetic principles with cultural psychology, linking architectural design to specific neural systems (visual, auditory, somatosensory, olfactory, vestibular, hippocampus, reward circuitry).",
    "The paper explicitly connects its findings to Attention Restoration Theory (ART) by discussing how nature exposure rejuvenates directed attention and memory.",
    "The paper explicitly connects its findings to Stress Reduction Theory (SRT) by discussing how natural scenes activate the parasympathetic nervous system to reduce stress."
  ],
  "methodological_critiques": [],
  "model_structure": "The proposed model is based on the aesthetic triad, where the sensory-motor system (processing fluency, complexity, naturalistic patterns) and the knowledge-meaning system (processing familiarity, expectations, context, cultural meaning) interact. This interaction is then uniformly moderated by the emotion valuation system, which acts as a regulator to balance feelings and emotions, leading to a balanced appreciation of aesthetic architecture. Culture and nature are presented as central elements influencing these systems and contributing to cognitive rejuvenation.",
